title "How the components interact: CMDB/Discovery"

# not modelled: "Ven" and "SLA" tags on the Tech Mgmt Service Offerings (vendor,
#   SLA), "Installed software" callout pointing at the servers, green frame around
#   the discovered CIs, Domains legend, "References data on record" legend

BC leaf-aa: Leaf Capability AA
BA app-a: Application A
BA app-b: Application B
BA app-c: Application C

SI app-a-prod: App A PROD
SI app-b-prod: App B PROD

BSO example-a: Example A
BSO example-b: Example B
BS bs-1: Service #1
SP portfolio-a: Portfolio A
SP portfolio-b: Portfolio B

TMS app-mgmt: App Mgmt Services
TMSO app-a-support: App A Support
TMSO app-b-support: App B Support

TMS compute: Compute/Hosting
TMSO windows-admin: Windows Administration
DCG all-win: All Win Servers
TMS database: Database Services
TMSO sql-support: SQL Support
DCG mssql-apps: MSSQL Apps
TMS network: Network Services
TMSO network-support: Network Support
DCG network-gear: Network Gear

CI(Application) appb-123: AppB@server123
CI(Application) appb-456: AppB@server456
CI(Server) server123: Server123
CI(Server) server456: Server456
CI(Database) mssql-123: MSSQL@server123
CI(Database) mssql-456: MSSQL@server456
CI(Switch) switch1001: Switch1001
CI(Router) router01: Router 01

leaf-aa -> app-a
leaf-aa -> app-b
leaf-aa -> app-c
app-a -> app-a-prod
app-b -> app-b-prod

# Portfolio A has a solid arrow into the Business Capability (not a standard CSDM pair; kept as shown).
portfolio-a -> leaf-aa
bs-1 -> portfolio-a
example-a -> bs-1
example-b -> bs-1
example-a -> app-b-prod
example-b -> app-a-prod

app-a-support -> app-mgmt
app-b-support -> app-mgmt
app-a-support -> app-a-prod
app-b-support -> app-b-prod

windows-admin -> compute
windows-admin -> all-win
all-win -> server123
all-win -> server456
sql-support -> database
sql-support -> mssql-apps
mssql-apps -> mssql-123
mssql-apps -> mssql-456
network-support -> network
network-support -> network-gear
network-gear -> switch1001
network-gear -> router01

# Service mapping
app-b-prod -> appb-123
app-b-prod -> appb-456
appb-123 -> server123 : Runs On
appb-456 -> server456 : Runs On
# Unlabelled arrows from each server down to its database instance (the
# Server456 connector passes behind MSSQL@server123 before reaching MSSQL@server456).
server123 -> mssql-123
server456 -> mssql-456

# Long connector from Portfolio B's left edge, routed around the CI frame, into Compute/Hosting.
compute -> portfolio-b
